Where inside the passive match the thread is

Run 576's panel said w8m33: the matching thread is inside the passive
match.  The passive match takes the entry's own registry lock to copy the
nub's properties, and a lock that somebody holds and does not let go is a
thread that never comes back.  That is the shape of the whole of it: the
matching thread is inside the NVRAM service's matching, the root nub's
matching -- the one our personality belongs to -- never comes round, and
the board waits for a driver that is waiting for the board.

So the waypoints go inside the passive match:

  35  the passive match was entered
  36  about to ask matchInternal
  37  matchInternal answered
  38  about to ask matchPropertyTable
  39  matchPropertyTable answered
  40  about to compare the name
  41  about to copy the nub's properties
  42  the properties were copied
  43  about to take the entry's registry lock
  44  the lock was taken

Which one it stands on is the line it is stuck in, and 43 without 44 is a
lock somebody is holding.

